{
  "title": "Parser: \"extra large\" without a hyphen stays in the item instead of becoming the size unit",
  "description": "\"extra-large\" is a size unit (units.rs SIZE_UNITS), but the unhyphenated spelling isn't: \"3 extra large eggs\" parses as item \"extra large eggs\" with no unit, and so do \"4 extra large ripe tomatoes, chopped\", \"4 extra large flour tortillas ((10 to 11-inch))\" and \"1 extra large egg yolk\" (pipeline fixtures). \
A bare count then weighs the default piece, not the extra-large one (eggs and shrimp have extra-large weights). \
Read \"extra large\" as the extra-large unit after an amount, the way measure.rs unit() reads \"extra-large\". \
Rerun make pipeline and check the fixture and data/ingredient-catalog-audit.md diffs. \
Server-side only (ramekin-core parser), so no web or iOS change.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
